Prevent stub profile nodes from orphaned D7 profile2 rows.

The profile-update migrations resolve their target node with a
migration_lookup against upgrade_d7_user_to_profile keyed on the profile2
row's uid, but without no_stub. D7 profile2 entities owned by a uid that has
no migrated profile -- uid 0 (anonymous) and uids deleted from {users} --
therefore cause Migrate to create a stub profile node, which Drupal fills
with generated sample values: a lorem ipsum first/last name and a
random@example.com address. Those stubs are published osu_profile nodes and
show up as bogus entries in the site directory.

Add no_stub: true so the lookup returns NULL instead of stubbing, and
skip_on_empty (method: row) so the orphaned profile2 row is dropped rather
than falling through to the entity:node destination with a NULL nid, which
would create a new node instead of updating an existing one.

--- a/modules/osu_user_to_profiles/migrations/upgrade_d7_user_profile_osu_person.yml
+++ b/modules/osu_user_to_profiles/migrations/upgrade_d7_user_profile_osu_person.yml
@@ -16,6 +16,10 @@
     - plugin: migration_lookup
       migration: upgrade_d7_user_to_profile
       source: uid
+      no_stub: true
+    - plugin: skip_on_empty
+      method: row
+      message: "No migrated profile node for this D7 uid; skipping orphaned profile2 row."
   field_profile_first_name:
     - plugin: get
       source: first_name
--- a/modules/osu_user_to_profiles/migrations/upgrade_d7_user_profile_osu_employee.yml
+++ b/modules/osu_user_to_profiles/migrations/upgrade_d7_user_profile_osu_employee.yml
@@ -14,6 +14,10 @@
